.TITLE "ipconfig"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays all current TCP/IP network configuration values and refreshes Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) and Domain Name System (DNS) settings.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**ipconfig**
Displays basic IP address, subnet mask, and default gateway for all adapters.
> 

**ipconfig /all**
Displays full TCP/IP configuration for all adapters.
> __/all__ detailed info flag

**ipconfig /release**
Releases the IPv4 address for the specified adapter.
> __/release__ DHCP release flag

**ipconfig /renew**
Renews the IPv4 address for the specified adapter.
> __/renew__ DHCP renew flag

**ipconfig /flushdns**
Purges the DNS Resolver cache.
> __/flushdns__ DNS flush flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __ipconfig /flushdns__ is a common troubleshooting step when a website fails to load despite having an active internet connection. Combine __/release__ and __/renew__ to resolve IP address conflicts.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:ping** **windows:netstat**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/ipconfig__
